The device function `reduceBlock` and the __global__ kernel
`reduceSinglePassMultiBlockCG` in main.cu are reproduced from:

    NVIDIA/cuda-samples,
    cpp/2_Concepts_and_Techniques/reductionMultiBlockCG/reductionMultiBlockCG.cu
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-samples/blob/master/cpp/2_Concepts_and_Techniques/reductionMultiBlockCG/reductionMultiBlockCG.cu
    Copyright (c) 2022, NVIDIA CORPORATION. All rights reserved.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

`reduceBlock` is reproduced completely unmodified. `reduceSinglePassMultiBlockCG`
is reproduced with one mechanical type change (the upstream kernel's
`float* g_idata`/`float* g_odata` parameters are `double*` here, so its
per-block partial sums are no longer truncated to float on the way to
global memory); no other line of either routine is changed. See the header
comment in main.cu for the full explanation.

